 and stays in `verificationMethod` with `revoked` set to the compromise time (CONVENTIONS.md §9.1). `rotateUpdateKey` — the identifier\'s update authority moves to a committed routine successor. `commitUpdateKey` — a new routine successor is committed. `replaceRecoveryCommitment` — the recovery commitment changes. `useRecoveryKey` — the change is authorized by the recovery key, which the identifier then reveals."},"role":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyRole"},"verificationMethod":{"type":"string"},"keyType":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyType"},"publicKeyMultibase":{"type":"string"},"commitment":{"type":"string"},"relationships":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DidVerificationRelationship"},"uniqueItems":true}}},"DidVerificationRelationship":{"title":"DidVerificationRelationship","type":"string","enum":["authentication","assertionMethod","keyAgreement","capabilityInvocation","capabilityDelegation"],"description":"A DID Core verification relationship."},"KeyRole":{"title":"KeyRole","type":"string","enum":["attestation","operational","messaging","update","authenticator"],"description":"The named key role a key occupies in an identity (CONVENTIONS.md §2; VTI-KEY-070 onward). `attestation` — the only keys in `assertionMethod`; sign the identity\'s attestation artefacts (credentials, endorsements, status lists) through the VTA\'s signing service and nowhere else. Generated inside the VTA, never derived, never exportable, never in a backup. `operational` — the only keys the identity\'s own process uses in `authentication`; sign the node\'s own traffic (Trust Task requests and responses, DIDComm and TSP signatures, invitations, notices, audit checkpoints). Derived. `messaging` — the only keys in `keyAgreement`; sign nothing. X25519, derived or generated in its own right and never converted from a signing key. `update` — the identifier\'s change authority as its DID method states it (a did:webvh log\'s `updateKeys` and `nextKeyHashes`, a KERI key event log\'s current and next keys); never a role-bound verification method, never in `keyRoles`. Generated inside the VTA, never derived, never exportable, never in a backup, and always accompanied by a committed recovery key held outside the VTA\'s protection boundary. `authenticator` — a key held on a person\'s own authenticator (a WebAuthn passkey), listed in `authentication` of that person\'s identity only; used only to verify the person\'s WebAuthn assertions (sign-in and step-up evidence) and never to accept a Data Integrity proof. The VTA never holds its private half, so it is enrolled by the passkey ceremony and never generated, added or rotated by these tasks. Never permitted on the durable identity of a VTA, a VTC or a VTN. No role permits `capabilityInvocation` or `capabilityDelegation` (VTI-KEY-075). The set is an extensible registry: a consumer that meets a role it does not implement MUST rely on the key for nothing, and MUST NOT map it onto a role it does know (VTI-KEY-074)."},"DidMethodName":{"title":"DidMethodName","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(:[a-z0-9]+)*\$","description":"The DID method an identity uses, as the method profile that governs it is named: `webvh` for a did:webvh identity, `scid:vh` for the did:scid:vh:1 form of one, `webs` for did:webs. Deliberately a pattern and not an enumeration: a method is added by publishing its profile under method-profiles/, never by changing this schema. A VTA MUST refuse a method it holds no profile for, or whose profile declares it ineligible, with `vta/dids:methodNotEligible`."},"KeyRoleChangeOutcome":{"title":"KeyRoleChangeOutcome","type":"string","enum":["preview","applied","pendingApproval","awaitingRecoveryProof"],"description":"`preview` — nothing was written; the response carries the plan. `applied` — the change was made (and published, unless `publication.selfPublish`). `pendingApproval` — the plan is recorded and awaits further approvals. `awaitingRecoveryProof` — the plan is approved and waits for the recovery custodian\'s proof (`preview.recoverySigning`); nothing is published until it arrives."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
